{
  "version": 1,
  "_note": "The telemetry QUEUE POLICY — the pure core every renderer shares (parity/F10-telemetry.md): the fingerprint fold, deterministic sampling, the bounded dedupe ring and the backoff schedule. It is pure on purpose: the platform half (on-disk persistence, the flush timer, the transport) differs per renderer, but WHICH events survive a crash loop and WHETHER a given event is sampled must not. A crash loop sends a COUNT, not ten thousand events; the bound drops the OLDEST and counts the drop, so the sink is told what it did not receive. Sampling is a pure function of the fingerprint (FNV-1a 32-bit, permille of 10000) rather than a random draw, so the same event is sampled the same way on every device and a corpus can pin it. Twins: kernel TelemetryQueuePolicy + TelemetryQueue (Swift Engine/iOS/TelemetryPolicy.swift · Kotlin :core TelemetryPolicy.kt · TS packages/kernel/src/telemetry.ts).",
  "fingerprint": [
    {
      "name": "a native crash with a moving address folds to one fingerprint",
      "source": "app",
      "code": "crash",
      "message": "SIGSEGV at 0x00007ff8 in Checkout",
      "expect": "app|crash|SIGSEGV at <addr> in Checkout"
    },
    {
      "name": "the same crash at another address folds identically",
      "source": "app",
      "code": "crash",
      "message": "SIGSEGV at 0x00001a2b in Checkout",
      "expect": "app|crash|SIGSEGV at <addr> in Checkout"
    },
    {
      "name": "an index error with a moving index folds",
      "source": "dom",
      "code": "render_failed",
      "message": "index 5 out of bounds for length 3",
      "expect": "dom|render_failed|index # out of bounds for length #"
    },
    {
      "name": "whitespace runs collapse",
      "source": "dom",
      "code": "render_failed",
      "message": "index   5    out of bounds",
      "expect": "dom|render_failed|index # out of bounds"
    },
    {
      "name": "an absent message is an empty tail",
      "source": "telemetry",
      "code": "queue_full",
      "message": null,
      "expect": "telemetry|queue_full|"
    },
    {
      "name": "a long message is capped at 200 characters",
      "source": "app",
      "code": "crash",
      "message": "",
      "expect": "app|crash|xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx"
    }
  ],
  "sampling": [
    {
      "fingerprint": "dom|render_failed|Checkout.dsx:#",
